  "summary": "Delays occur most frequently in the handoff from admission to VTE prophylaxis, where 28.6 % (11.7–54.6 %) of cases breached the 24-hour target. System issues account for 21.4 % of these delays, primarily due to VTE prophylaxis not being prescribed. The handoff from hypoxaemia to admission showed no breaches, but data quality issues limited analysis. The handoff from discharge to follow-up also showed no breaches, but again, data quality issues were present. Overall, system factors are the main driver of delays where they occur.",
